<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-NATAL BEAT E.P. BY INNINGS AND 46 RUNS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NATAL BEAT E.P. BY INNINGS AND 46 RUNS.</headline>
<dateline>PORT ELIZABETH 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A stunning batting</p>
<p>collapse by Eastern Province saw Natal romp to an innings</p>
<p>victory with a little more than a day to spare in their</p>
<p>Supersport series cricket match at St George's Park on Sunday.</p>
<p>Facing a first innings deficit of 164 E.P. slumped to a</p>
<p>disappointing 118 for nine with 6.3 overs left in the day to</p>
<p>lose by and innings and 46 runs.</p>
<p>Number 11 batsman Mornantau Hayward was unable to bat</p>
<p>because of an injured knee.</p>
<p>Natal spinners Pat Symcox (four for 26) and Derek Crookes</p>
<p>(three for 27) wrecked havoc with the home sides second innings</p>
<p>to secure victory after Natal made 429 in their first innings in</p>
<p>reply to E.P.'s 265.</p>
<p>In that innings both Errol Stewart (138) and Jonty Rhodes</p>
<p>(108) hit centuries in a record Natal third wicket stand of 235.</p>
<p>Aggressive batting from Natal's lower order helped the visitors</p>
<p>take what ultimately proved to be a match winning first innings</p>
<p>ead. </p>
